---
title: Turkey Larb Lettuce Wraps
course: main
cuisine: thai
servings: 4
time_active: 25
time_total: 30
leftovers: good
tags: [weeknight, quick]
description: Thai-style ground turkey and mushrooms with lime, fish sauce, ginger, and cilantro, in lettuce cups with jasmine rice on the side.
---

Start @jasmine rice{1 1/2%cups} in a #rice cooker{} or pot.

Whisk together @fish sauce{3%tbsp}, the juice of @limes{3}, @honey{2%tsp}, and @red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp}.

Heat @neutral oil{1%tbsp} in a large #skillet{} over medium-high. Add @mushrooms{8%oz}(cremini, finely chopped) and cook, stirring now and then, until their liquid cooks off and they brown, ~{6-8%minutes}.

Add @ground turkey{1%lb} and cook, breaking it into small crumbles, until no longer pink, ~{5-6%minutes}.

Add @shallots{2}(thinly sliced), @ginger{1%tbsp}(grated), and @garlic{2%clove}(minced). Cook until the shallots soften, ~{2%minutes}. Take the pan off the heat.

Pour in the dressing and toss. Let it cool a couple of minutes, then fold in @cilantro{3/4%cup}(chopped) and @scallions{3}(thinly sliced). Taste: it should be sour, salty, and a little spicy. Add more lime or fish sauce to get there.

Spoon into leaves of @butter lettuce{2%head}(or little gem) and serve with the rice.

> For leftovers, store the filling apart from the lettuce. It's good cold or warm over rice for lunch. Keeps 3 days.
